+## Missing context
+
+Task 3 cannot be finished within its `scope` as planned.
+
+The change's own "Entry paths exist" requirement makes `lintChangeFolder`
+report an error for a task whose `entry` no tree provides. Task 1's runtime
+tests, in `tests/entry-missing-run.test.ts`, deliberately approve exactly such
+a change and expect `approve` to succeed so the watcher can then kill the task
+with `entry_missing`:
+
+- `tests/entry-missing-run.test.ts:56` — writes task 1 `entry: [src/gone.ts]`,
+  then `assertOk(await project.approve(), 'approve')`.
+- `tests/entry-missing-run.test.ts:90` — same first approve, before the entry is
+  revised.
+- `tests/entry-missing-run.test.ts:140` — the `src/*.rs` row writes
+  `entry: [src/*.rs]` with no matching file and expects approve to succeed.
+
+Once task 3 adds the lint error, all three `approve` calls fail, so the
+proposal-level `verify` (`pnpm verify`, which runs `tests/**/*.test.ts`) is red
+at this task's boundary. The prior attempt died with exactly this
+`change_verify_red` dead marker (`.run/dead/3.1.md`).
+
+`tests/entry-missing-run.test.ts` is not in this task's `scope`, and this task
+sets no `tests.modify`, so I may not change it. There is no spec-compliant way
+to make both the new lint error and those tests pass: the two scenarios are the
+same change and differ only in which entrypoint reaches them, and no
+provided-path rule (change folder, own/earlier scope, default-branch tip,
+pattern match, approved other-change scope) can distinguish them.
+
+## Blocked
+
+The plan must be revised before task 3 can pass its change-level verify.
+Task 1's runtime scenarios and task 3's lint error are mutually exclusive as
+the change is written today: to prove the watcher's `entry_missing` path the
+tests must get a change approved with a missing `entry`, but approval lints and
+now rejects it.
+
+What I need:
+
+1. `tests/entry-missing-run.test.ts` added to task 3's `scope`, with
+   `tests.modify: true`, so task 3 can rewrite how those tests reach an
+   approved change whose task entry is missing without calling `approve` on a
+   missing entry. For example, approve with a valid `entry: []` (or commit the
+   entry file only to the worktree after approval) and then commit the
+   `tasks/1.md` edit that names the missing file in the worktree with the
+   `git()` helper `tests/recovery-support.ts` exports, so the watcher's runtime
+   check (not lint) kills the task. The `src/*.rs` and `src/gone.ts` rows need
+   the same treatment.
+2. Alternatively, the planner can split the runtime proof of
+   "Entry names a removed file", "Steered task runs", and the negative row of
+   "Entries that count as present" out of `tests/entry-missing-run.test.ts`
+   into a new file task 3 owns, and have task 3 remove the conflicting rows
+   from task 1's file under `tests.modify: true`. Either way the shared file
+   must be in task 3's `scope` and identified in the proposal.
+
+I did not change any file, so the plan and the tree are exactly as this task
+received them.
